# TPSS on helium -- the smallest deck on a META-GGA functional.
#
# A meta-gga depends on the kinetic energy density
#
#     tau_sigma = 1/2 sum_i |grad psi_i|^2
#
# which is built from the orbitals, not from the density. Because tau is an
# orbital functional there is no closed-form dE_xc/drho, so the tau dependence
# enters the Kohn-Sham operator as a non-multiplicative term
#
#     v_tau psi_i = -1/2 grad.( (de_xc/dtau) grad psi_i )
#
# i.e. a position-dependent inverse effective mass, 1 + de_xc/dtau, inside the
# kinetic operator. That term is applied to the orbitals alongside exact
# exchange rather than folded into the local potential, so this deck is the one
# that exercises it.
#
# TPSS first, deliberately: it is built on z = tau_W/tau, and so does not carry
# the oscillation in grad(de/dtau) near alpha = 1 that makes the SCAN family
# grid-hungry. `r2scan` and `scan` are also available as aliases.
#
# Run:   ./run.sh          (or: madqc scf_he_tpss.in)

dft
    xc       tpss
    maxiter  20
    econv    1e-4
    dconv    1e-3
end

molecule
    units   atomic
    eprec   1e-6
    He  0.0  0.0  0.0
end
